Sources:
- BGS World Data Centre for Geomagnetism (Edinburgh), Worldwide Observatory Annual Means; values
  supplied by the observatory operators
  <https://geomag.bgs.ac.uk/data_service/data/annual_means.shtml>
- BGS World Data Centre for Geomagnetism (Edinburgh), Global Survey Data (repeat stations and
  one-off stations), via the WDC API; values supplied by national survey institutes
  <https://wdcapi.bgs.ac.uk/global-geomagnetic-survey>
- IAGA, International Geomagnetic Reference Field, 14th generation (IGRF-14) coefficients
  <https://www.ngdc.noaa.gov/IAGA/vmod/coeffs/igrf14coeffs.txt>
Evidence class (rule 10): check
Where the Earth's radius enters:
- IGRF-14 (igrf14coeffs.txt): magnetic latitude from the IGRF pole, a model fitted on the globe; the
  measured I and F themselves carry no radius
What would vindicate the flat model (rule 5): A flat residual box centred on zero and as narrow as
  the globe's, with the same median north and south of the magnetic equator; or a field-strength box
  narrower than every globe box.
